{
    "background_story": "Pancake was a laid-back feline who spent most of his days lounging in the sunbeams that streamed through the windows. However, beneath his calm exterior lay a short fuse. Whenever his human, a quirky artist, would attempt to dress him up in ridiculous costumes, Pancake's apoplectiform tendencies would surface. His face would turn beet red, his ears would fold back, and he would emit a low, rumbling growl that sent shivers down the spines of anyone within earshot. It was as if he was on the verge of bursting a blood vessel from sheer indignation. Despite his explosive outbursts, Pancake's human adored him, recognizing that his tantrums were a sign of his passionate and intense personality. After all, who needs a placid cat when you can have one that's as fiery as a sparkler on the 4th of July?",
